-- A TYPICALLY that nothing evaluates must be a literal. A written ASSUME's is
-- not used (W6 is deferred), so an expression there would be a default that
-- quietly does nothing. A section input's, a rule input's and a record field's
-- are evaluated, and take an expression (ok/typically-expression.l4).

-- ERROR: not a literal (a compound expression)
ASSUME flag IS A BOOLEAN TYPICALLY (TRUE AND FALSE)
